      "writtenOn": "2022-11-11T21:12:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems a little silly, when all we really want is for header files to be treated like any other regular source file, just compiled with `-xc++` (or more verbosely, `--language c++`). Is there any way we can tell Bazel to just do that? It seems a bit weird to try to hack in particular files like this.",
      "revId": "b1d06473c075fb1dd0866aa757660c212e820a73",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
